  "title": "Galen",
  "summary": "Galen (129–c. 200 or 216 CE) was a Greek physician and medical author from Pergamon, where in 157 he became doctor to the gladiators. Moving to Rome in the early 160s, he served as court physician to the emperors Marcus Aurelius, Commodus and Septimius Severus. He held anatomy to be the foundation of medicine and taught dissection, carried out on animals. His many books were widely read in Byzantium and the Arab world, and Ibn Sina and Vesalius built on them.",
